@startuml GupShup Cafe - Communication Diagram (Real-time Events)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title GupShup Cafe - Real-time Communication Flow (Socket.io Events)

component "React App\n(User A)" as ClientA
component "React App\n(User B)" as ClientB
component "React App\n(User C)" as ClientC
component "AWS Fargate\n(FastAPI + Socket.io)" as Backend
component "Room Manager" as RoomMgr
component "Database\n(SQLite)" as DB
component "AWS Strands\nOrchestrator" as LLM

' Connection events
ClientA -> Backend : **1. connect**\n{auth_token}
Backend -> ClientA : **1.1 connected**\n{socket_id}

ClientB -> Backend : **2. connect**\n{auth_token}
Backend -> ClientB : **2.1 connected**\n{socket_id}

ClientC -> Backend : **3. connect**\n{auth_token}
Backend -> ClientC : **3.1 connected**\n{socket_id}

' Room creation
ClientA -> Backend : **4. create-room**\n{name, topic, max_participants}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **4.1** create_room()
RoomMgr -> DB : **4.2** INSERT session
DB -> RoomMgr : **4.3** session_id
RoomMgr -> Backend : **4.4** Room created
Backend -> ClientA : **4.5 room-created**\n{room_code, config}

' Join room
ClientB -> Backend : **5. join-room**\n{room_code, anonymous_name}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **5.1** join_room()
RoomMgr -> DB : **5.2** INSERT participant
DB -> RoomMgr : **5.3** participant_id
RoomMgr -> Backend : **5.4** Participant added

Backend -> ClientA : **5.5 participant-joined**\n{participant: UserB}
Backend -> ClientB : **5.6 participant-joined**\n{participant: UserB}

Backend -> ClientA : **5.7 participants-update**\n{participants: [A, B]}
Backend -> ClientB : **5.8 participants-update**\n{participants: [A, B]}

ClientC -> Backend : **6. join-room**\n{room_code, anonymous_name}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **6.1** join_room()
RoomMgr -> DB : **6.2** INSERT participant
RoomMgr -> Backend : **6.3** Participant added

Backend -> ClientA : **6.4 participant-joined**\n{participant: UserC}
Backend -> ClientB : **6.5 participant-joined**\n{participant: UserC}
Backend -> ClientC : **6.6 participant-joined**\n{participant: UserC}

Backend -> ClientA : **6.7 participants-update**\n{participants: [A, B, C]}
Backend -> ClientB : **6.8 participants-update**\n{participants: [A, B, C]}
Backend -> ClientC : **6.9 participants-update**\n{participants: [A, B, C]}

' Ready status
ClientA -> Backend : **7. ready**\n{room_code}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **7.1** set_participant_ready()
RoomMgr -> Backend : **7.2** Ready updated

Backend -> ClientA : **7.3 participant-ready**\n{participant_id: A}
Backend -> ClientB : **7.4 participant-ready**\n{participant_id: A}
Backend -> ClientC : **7.5 participant-ready**\n{participant_id: A}

ClientB -> Backend : **8. ready**\n{room_code}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **8.1** set_participant_ready()
Backend -> ClientA : **8.2 participant-ready**\n{participant_id: B}
Backend -> ClientB : **8.3 participant-ready**\n{participant_id: B}
Backend -> ClientC : **8.4 participant-ready**\n{participant_id: B}

ClientC -> Backend : **9. ready**\n{room_code}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **9.1** set_participant_ready()
RoomMgr -> RoomMgr : **9.2** Check all_ready()
RoomMgr -> Backend : **9.3** All ready = true

Backend -> ClientA : **9.4 all-ready**\n{can_start: true}
Backend -> ClientB : **9.5 all-ready**\n{can_start: true}
Backend -> ClientC : **9.6 all-ready**\n{can_start: true}

' Start discussion
ClientA -> Backend : **10. start-discussion**\n{room_code}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **10.1** start_discussion()
RoomMgr -> DB : **10.2** UPDATE session status
RoomMgr -> Backend : **10.3** Discussion started

Backend -> ClientA : **10.4 discussion-started**\n{room_state}
Backend -> ClientB : **10.5 discussion-started**\n{room_state}
Backend -> ClientC : **10.6 discussion-started**\n{room_state}

Backend -> ClientA : **10.7 turn-started**\n{speaker_index: 0, timer: 60}
Backend -> ClientB : **10.8 turn-started**\n{speaker_index: 0, timer: 60}
Backend -> ClientC : **10.9 turn-started**\n{speaker_index: 0, timer: 60}

' WebRTC signaling (simplified)
note over ClientA, ClientB
  **WebRTC Signaling Events**
  (See WebRTC sequence diagram for details)
end note

ClientA -> Backend : **11. webrtc-offer**\n{target: B, offer}
Backend -> ClientB : **11.1 webrtc-offer**\n{from: A, offer}

ClientB -> Backend : **12. webrtc-answer**\n{target: A, answer}
Backend -> ClientA : **12.1 webrtc-answer**\n{from: B, answer}

ClientA -> Backend : **13. webrtc-ice-candidate**\n{target: B, candidate}
Backend -> ClientB : **13.1 webrtc-ice-candidate**\n{from: A, candidate}

' Speech and feedback
ClientA -> Backend : **14. speech-transcript**\n{text: "I thinks AI...", speaker: A}
Backend -> DB : **14.1** INSERT transcript
Backend -> LLM : **14.2** get_english_feedback(instant=true)
LLM -> Backend : **14.3** Feedback result (2-3s)
Backend -> DB : **14.4** INSERT feedback
Backend -> ClientA : **14.5 english-feedback**\n{grammar: [...], cefr: B1} (PRIVATE)

note right of Backend
  Private feedback sent
  only to ClientA's socket
  (not broadcast to B or C)
end note

' Turn management
Backend -> ClientA : **15. timer-warning**\n{remaining: 10s}
Backend -> ClientB : **15.1 timer-warning**\n{remaining: 10s}
Backend -> ClientC : **15.2 timer-warning**\n{remaining: 10s}

ClientA -> Backend : **16. end-turn**\n{room_code}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **16.1** next_speaker()
RoomMgr -> RoomMgr : **16.2** Increment speaker_index
RoomMgr -> Backend : **16.3** Next speaker: B

Backend -> ClientA : **16.4 turn-ended**\n{speaker: A}
Backend -> ClientB : **16.5 turn-ended**\n{speaker: A}
Backend -> ClientC : **16.6 turn-ended**\n{speaker: A}

Backend -> ClientA : **16.7 turn-started**\n{speaker_index: 1, timer: 60}
Backend -> ClientB : **16.8 turn-started**\n{speaker_index: 1, timer: 60}
Backend -> ClientC : **16.9 turn-started**\n{speaker_index: 1, timer: 60}

' Round completion
note over Backend, RoomMgr
  After all speakers finish,
  round advances
end note

Backend -> ClientA : **17. round-complete**\n{round: 1, next: 2}
Backend -> ClientB : **17.1 round-complete**\n{round: 1, next: 2}
Backend -> ClientC : **17.2 round-complete**\n{round: 1, next: 2}

' Discussion end
note over RoomMgr
  After 3 rounds complete
end note

RoomMgr -> Backend : **18** Discussion complete
Backend -> DB : **18.1** UPDATE session (ended_at)
Backend -> LLM : **18.2** get_english_feedback(instant=false)
LLM -> Backend : **18.3** Comprehensive analysis
Backend -> DB : **18.4** INSERT comprehensive feedback

Backend -> ClientA : **18.5 discussion-ended**\n{session_id}
Backend -> ClientB : **18.6 discussion-ended**\n{session_id}
Backend -> ClientC : **18.7 discussion-ended**\n{session_id}

Backend -> ClientA : **18.8 session-summary**\n{feedback, stats}
Backend -> ClientB : **18.9 session-summary**\n{feedback, stats}
Backend -> ClientC : **18.10 session-summary**\n{feedback, stats}

' Leave room
ClientA -> Backend : **19. leave-room**\n{room_code}
Backend -> RoomMgr : **19.1** remove_participant()
RoomMgr -> DB : **19.2** UPDATE participant (left_at)
RoomMgr -> Backend : **19.3** Participant removed

Backend -> ClientB : **19.4 participant-left**\n{participant_id: A}
Backend -> ClientC : **19.5 participant-left**\n{participant_id: A}

Backend -> ClientB : **19.6 participants-update**\n{participants: [B, C]}
Backend -> ClientC : **19.7 participants-update**\n{participants: [B, C]}

' Disconnect
ClientA -> Backend : **20. disconnect**
Backend -> Backend : **20.1** Cleanup connections

note as EventSummary
  **Socket.io Event Categories:**
  
  **Connection Management:**
  - connect, connected, disconnect
  
  **Room Operations:**
  - create-room, room-created
  - join-room, participant-joined
  - leave-room, participant-left
  - participants-update
  
  **Discussion Control:**
  - ready, participant-ready, all-ready
  - start-discussion, discussion-started
  - turn-started, turn-ended
  - round-complete, discussion-ended
  - timer-warning
  
  **WebRTC Signaling:**
  - webrtc-offer, webrtc-answer
  - webrtc-ice-candidate
  - participant-muted, participant-unmuted
  
  **Speech & Feedback:**
  - speech-transcript
  - english-feedback (private)
  - agent-message
  - session-summary
  
  **Error Handling:**
  - error, room-full, room-not-found
  - invalid-action, unauthorized
end note

note as BroadcastPatterns
  **Event Broadcasting Patterns:**
  
  **1. To All in Room (broadcast):**
  ```python
  await sio.emit('participants-update',
                 data,
                 room=room_code)
  ```
  - participant-joined/left
  - turn-started/ended
  - discussion-started/ended
  
  **2. To Specific User (private):**
  ```python
  await sio.emit('english-feedback',
                 data,
                 room=socket_id)
  ```
  - english-feedback
  - personal-message
  
  **3. To All Except Sender:**
  ```python
  await sio.emit('participant-ready',
                 data,
                 room=room_code,
                 skip_sid=sender_sid)
  ```
  - Used for echoing confirmations
  
  **4. To Specific Peer (WebRTC):**
  ```python
  await sio.emit('webrtc-offer',
                 data,
                 room=target_socket_id)
  ```
  - webrtc-offer/answer
  - webrtc-ice-candidate
end note

note as PerformanceConsiderations
  **Real-time Performance:**
  
  **Socket.io Configuration:**
  - Transport: WebSocket (prefer over polling)
  - Ping interval: 25s
  - Ping timeout: 60s
  - Max buffer size: 1MB
  
  **Event Payload Size:**
  - Keep small (<10KB per event)
  - Use participant IDs (not full objects)
  - Compress large data
  
  **Room Scaling:**
  - Max 6 participants per room
  - 100s of concurrent rooms supported
  - Fargate auto-scales on CPU
  
  **WebRTC Optimization:**
  - P2P audio (no server relay)
  - Reduces backend bandwidth
  - Better latency (<100ms)
  
  **Database Impact:**
  - Async SQLite on EFS
  - Connection pooling
  - Batch inserts for transcripts
  - Non-blocking I/O
end note

@enduml
